79098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2026-10-07T03:36:30Z","updated_at":"2026-10-07T20:50:03Z","closed_at":"2026-10-07T20:49:56Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested Versions\n\n4.7.2.stable\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11, RTX 4080 Laptop / Android (Samsung S25 FE), Mobile renderer (Vulkan)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using the Mobile renderer, moving `GPUParticlesCollisionHeightField3D` (e.g. with `follow_camera_enabled = true`) leaves trails behind obstacles. It seems the heightfield texture is never cleared between updates, causing previous collision data to smear along movement.\n\nThis does not happen in Forward+.\n\nIt looks like the fix from #102133 was applied to `render_forward_clustered.cpp`, but the Mobile equivalent in `render_forward_mobile.cpp` is missing `RD::DRAW_CLEAR_ALL`.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Run the attached MRP with the Mobile renderer.\n2. Observe particles landing in mid-air on the smeared trail left behind by the bump.\n3. Switch to Forward+ to see correct behavior.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[heightfield_mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/33170576/heightfield_mrp.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.